  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nThrough Saturday: continued dry and noticeably cooler. Latest \nsatellite imagery/RAP analysis showed a shortwave rounding the base \nof a closed upper level low spinning over the Great Lakes region. \nThis shortwave will help support a >1020mb surface high drop \nsoutheast into our region while supporting a dry cold front move \nthrough our CWA. This dry cold front was already south of Highway 82 \nand will push southeast of our CWA early this evening. In its wake \ncooler and drier air will filter into the CWA. Normal morning lows \nrun in the 40s but our north and central sites will likely bottom \nout a degree or two cooler than normal. Saturday the shortwave \ntrough will continue east of our CWA leaving near zonal flow aloft \nwhile the surface high to the north continues to push into the CWA. \nOur normal highs run from the mid 60s north to the lower 70s south. \nAfternoon highs Saturday will run from the lower 60s north to the \nlower 70s south. /22/\n\nMuch cooler temperatures will continue through Sunday night, and\nthis will support the potential for patchy areas of frost over\nnorth central into northeast MS both Sat night and Sun night. The\ndry soil conditions will support overachieving of the nocturnal \ncooling processes. At the same time, we'll have to consider the \npotential for cirrus cloud decks, which could keep temperatures \nfrom dropping as much. Putting these factors together yields \nuncertainty for low temperatures and potential frost impacts. We \nare maintaining the current limited frost threat in our \nmessaging for Sat night and Sun night.\n\nEarly to mid next week: Quiet, cloudy and mostly dry pattern will\npersist into the following week. Eastward ejection of upper low \nis slower than yesterday morning, with the center over west TX. \nThis will keep moist, isentropic ascent and cloudy conditions\ndraped across the Gulf Coast states through at least mid week \n(Wednesday). Cannot rule out an isolated rain shower during this \ntime but with upper low filling in and becoming more open wave,\nascent will be less as it propagates eastward. With some thermal \ntemps warming, highs will moderate from seasonable early week to \nseasonably warm mid week (68F to 76F Monday to 70F to 78F by \nWednesday). Lows will remain seasonably cool but gradually less \ncold. The synoptic pattern becomes less confident in late week:\nsynoptic amplitude becomes less confident in western zone of jet\nenergy across the Plains from the GFS while the Euro shows more\ndeep mean troughing for areas east of the Plains. Cluster analysis\nindicate a good percentage of members from the ECENS and GEFS (30\nto 45 percent) favor a clusters/pattern closer to the Euro, GEFS\nand AI (global model suite and ensemble). This favors a drier and\ncooler pattern into late week. Will have to monitor the synoptic\nsetup for increased wildfire danger as gradient winds could\nincrease in a well-mixed dry boundary layer by Friday. /DC/EC/",
